---
import avatar from '@/assets/avatar.jpeg'
import { Card } from 'astro-pure/user'
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/CommonPage.astro'
import Substats from '@/components/about/Substats.astro'
import ToolSection from '@/components/about/ToolSection.astro'
import config from '@/site-config'
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'experiences', text: 'Experiences' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'tools', text: 'Tools' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'social-networks', text: 'Social Networks' },
]
---

<PageLayout title='About' {headings} info={{ slug: '/about', hideComment: true }}>
  <Image
        src={avatar}
        alt='profile'
        class='h-33 w-auto border p-1'
        loading='eager'
      />
  <p>Software Engineer · Graduate Student (Data Science)</p>
  <p>
    Hey, I'm {config.author} — a software engineer and graduate student based in Bali, Indonesia. 
    I've spent the last seven-plus years building web and mobile apps across different industries, 
    picking up a fair share of lessons along the way. My bachelor's in Information Technology came 
    from Universitas Udayana, which gave me the fundamentals that still anchor my work today.
  </p>
  <p>Day to day, I write code mostly in Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, and Dart — bouncing between 
    Angular, React, Flutter, and Spring Boot depending on what the project calls for. I care about 
    code that holds up over time: readable, tested, and not over-engineered. Whether it's a 
    customer-facing app or an internal enterprise tool, I try to keep things practical and 
    focused on what actually matters for the people using it.</p>
  <p>As of mid-2026, I'm also back in school — pursuing a Master's in Information Technology 
    with a concentration in Data Science. My research revolves around Retrieval-Augmented 
    Generation (RAG), large language models, and token optimization. Specifically, I'm looking 
    at how to make RAG pipelines more efficient without sacrificing answer quality — because 
    sending thousands of tokens per query adds up fast, and most of it isn't doing real work. 
    It's a space that moves quickly, and honestly, that's what makes it interesting.</p>

  <h2 id="experiences">Experiences</h2>
  <div class='flex flex-1 flex-col gap-y-3'>
    <Card
      heading='PT. Sigma Cipta Caraka (Telkomsigma)'
      subheading='Programmer'
      date='Feb 2019 - Present'
      />
    <Card
      heading='Patala Stock'
      subheading='Fullstack Developer'
      date='Feb 2024 - Jul 2024'
    />
    <Card
      heading='AW Bali Web Design and Development'
      subheading='Fullstack Programmer'
      date='Oct 2018 - Jan 2019'
      />
    <Card
      heading='AyoAntre.com'
      subheading='Fullstack Programmer'
      date='Mar 2018 - Sep 2018'
    />
  </Section> 

